@DateFrom = 2024-04-01
@DateTo = 2024-04-12
### Mint Google ID token (run this first; token is valid ~1h)
# @name MintToken
POST https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&client_id={{Google_ClientId}}&client_secret={{Google_ClientSecret}}&refresh_token={{Google_RefreshToken}}


// Auth contracts (ADR-0003): AGENT requests carry the key in BOTH X-Api-Key
// (in-app middleware) and Authorization (gateway identity source). HUMAN
// requests carry the Google ID token in BOTH Authorization as "Bearer <token>"
// (gateway identity source → Google validator at the edge) and
// x-google-idtoken (in-app middleware). Paths never fall back into each other.

### AI Extract Method
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/AI/extract
Accept: */*
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{Agent_ApiKey}}
Authorization: {{Agent_ApiKey}}

{
  "Language": "en-US",
  "Prompt": "Create an expense for today with the amount of 10. It was spent on a cafeteria named Ho Ho."
}

### Match Expenses
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/Expense/match/
Accept: */*
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{Agent_ApiKey}}
Authorization: {{Agent_ApiKey}}

### List Account Transactions
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/Account/transactions/?dateFrom={{DateFrom}}&dateTo={{DateTo}}
Accept: */*
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{Agent_ApiKey}}
Authorization: {{Agent_ApiKey}}

### Create Expense
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/Expense/
Accept: */*
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{Agent_ApiKey}}
Authorization: {{Agent_ApiKey}}

{
  "date": "2024-03-19T12:15:42.953Z",
  "amount": 10,
  "description": "Dote",
  "category": "Eating out"
}

### List Latest Expenses
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/Expense/latest/5
Accept: */*
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{Agent_ApiKey}}
Authorization: {{Agent_ApiKey}}

### List Categories
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/Category/
Accept: */*
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{Agent_ApiKey}}
Authorization: {{Agent_ApiKey}}

### Health Check (public — no auth needed)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/healthz/
Accept: */*

### Human: List Latest Expenses (Google ID token in BOTH headers)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/Expense/latest/5
Accept: */*
x-google-idtoken: {{MintToken.response.body.$.id_token}}
Authorization: Bearer {{Mint...en}}

### Human: Create Expense (Google ID token in BOTH headers)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/Expense/
Accept: */*
Content-Type: application/json
x-google-idtoken: {{Google_IdToken}}
Authorization: Bearer {{Google_IdToken}}

{
  "date": "2024-03-19T12:15:42.953Z",
  "amount": 10,
  "description": "Dote",
  "category": "Eating out"
}
// Smoke scope (ADR-0009): any authenticated caller may add "X-Sheet-Scope: smoke"
// to redirect writes AND list reads to the environment's Smoke Test tab. The
// integration suite uses it so deployed smokes never touch real tabs. POST
// /Expense returns the opaque Expense Id; DELETE /Smoke/{id} removes that row
// (read-before-delete, 404 when gone) and is scoped to the smoke tab by the
// route itself — it needs no X-Sheet-Scope header.

### Smoke: Create Expense (writes to the Smoke Test tab, returns Expense Id)
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/Expense/
Accept: */*
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{Agent_ApiKey}}
Authorization: {{Agent_ApiKey}}
X-Sheet-Scope: smoke

{
  "date": "2024-03-19T12:15:42.953Z",
  "amount": 0.01,
  "description": "integration test",
  "category": "Integration Tests"
}

### Smoke: List Latest Expenses (reads the Smoke Test tab)
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/Expense/latest/5
Accept: */*
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{Agent_ApiKey}}
Authorization: {{Agent_ApiKey}}
X-Sheet-Scope: smoke

### Smoke: Delete Expense row by Id (Route-scoped to the Smoke Test tab; 404 when gone)
DELETE {{Api_HostAddress}}/Smoke/5
Accept: */*
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{Agent_ApiKey}}
Authorization: {{Agent_ApiKey}}